&lt;h2 id="the-end">&lt;a href="#the-end" class="header-anchor">&lt;/a>The End
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>ToaruOS was a really cool OS, and I thoroughly enjoyed hacking through it! Despite this being a baby challenge, I learned a lot about OS development and x86_64 in doing it. Though none of that would be apparent from this write-up, as most of what I learned ended up being unnecessary for the exploit I found 🙃&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Funnily enough, I later learned that Josh had independently discovered the same vulnerability earlier, though he didn&amp;rsquo;t exploit it. He also found another cool one that involves a physical use-after-free which he did &lt;a class="link" href="https://joshsteffen.com/posts/hxp-38c3-ctf-ser-szwajcarski/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
>exploit and write about&lt;/a>!&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>